Public LMS patch for mPDF 8.3.1 (ADR-052). Applied by bin/prefix-vendor.sh to a
fresh mPDF from Composer, before Strauss prefixes it; `git apply` stops the build
if any hunk no longer applies, for example after an mPDF version bump. Every mPDF
upgrade must re-apply this patch and re-run the certificate tests and matrix.

Why: current Noto Sans builds (fontmake) use OpenType structures mPDF 8.3.1's
font reader and shaper reject or mishandle. With this patch, Noto Sans Arabic,
Hebrew, Devanagari, Bengali, Tamil and Thai load and shape correctly.

1. GSUB lookup type 5 (contextual substitution), format 3 (coverage-based).
   OpenType: SequenceContextFormat3 = format, glyphCount, seqLookupCount,
   coverageOffsets[glyphCount] (Offset16 from the subtable), then
   seqLookupRecords[seqLookupCount] (sequenceIndex, lookupListIndex).
   TTFontFile read it into nothing and threw "GPOS Lookup Type 5, Format 3 not
   supported"; its builder threw "not tested"; Otl threw "not TESTED YET".
   Read and applied as chained context format 3 (type 6.3) with no backtrack
   or lookahead. Fonts: Noto Sans Arabic, Devanagari, Bengali.
   Upstream: mpdf/mpdf discussion #1957 (Noto Naskh Arabic, same error).
2. GDEF mark glyph sets (MarkGlyphSetsDef) and lookup flag 0x0010
   (useMarkFilteringSet). OpenType: MarkGlyphSetsDef = format, markGlyphSetCount,
   coverageOffsets[] (Offset32 from the start of MarkGlyphSetsDef). A lookup
   with the flag ignores every mark NOT in its set. mPDF threw "not supported"
   / "Not tested yet"; behind the throws, it seeked to each coverage offset as
   if it were absolute and stored the set itself as the marks to ignore.
   Fixed: offset = GDEF + MarkGlyphSetsDef + coverage offset; stored string =
   all marks (GlyphClassDef class 3) minus the set, like mPDF's mark attachment
   classes; the "no set given" check is strict, because set 0 == '' on PHP 7.
   Fonts: Noto Sans Tamil, Thai. Upstream: mpdf/mpdf#1408 (closed as
   unsupported); the same fix, checked against HarfBuzz hb-shape, is
   GravityPDF/mpdf#14 (fork, merged 2026-09-07).
3. Reader crashes: contextual builders count the `subs` of the lookups they
   call, which are unset when that lookup is itself contextual (TypeError on
   PHP 8, Noto Sans Bengali); the Indic `locl` collector read `replace` from
   contextual rules, which have none (warning).
4. Arabic joining forms that are 1-to-n substitutions (GSUB type 2 under
   init/medi/fina): Noto draws Farsi yeh and kaf as a dotless body plus a dots
   mark. mPDF stored the form as "0E008 0E06E" and the joining shaper used it
   as one code point, so the letter was blank. The shaper now inserts every
   glyph as GSUB type 2 does; the RTL glyph list and the kashida finals take
   the parts too.
5. WebP without GD: processWebp() called imagecreatefromstring() before
   checking it exists, a fatal Error on a server without GD. Now the image is
   left out, like mPDF's other GD paths.

The "PublicLMS patch:" comments mark each change for review.

